-small-bathroom-counter">How do I decorate a small bathroom counter?</a></li><li><a class="kb-table-of-contents__entry" href="#how-do-i-make-my-bathroom-counter-look-expensive">How do I make my bathroom counter look expensive?</a></li><li><a class="kb-table-of-contents__entry" href="#should-i-keep-medicines-on-the-bathroom-counter">Should I keep medicines on the bathroom counter?</a></li></ul></li><li><a class="kb-table-of-contents__entry" href="#final-thoughts">Final Thoughts</a></li></ul></div></nav>


<h2 class="wp-block-heading">Bathroom Counter Zones</h2>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph">A bathroom counter has three jobs: washing, getting ready and looking nice. Give each one its own spot. The area around the sink and faucet gets splashed, so keep it clear. One tray beside the sink holds the daily items, and one corner holds the decor.</p>



