<p class="wp-block-paragraph">For more ways to tame bathroom clutter, see our <a href="https://dailyspacehacks.com/bathroom-organization-ideas/">bathroom organization ideas</a>.</p>



<h2 class="wp-block-heading">Frequently Asked Questions</h2>



<h3 class="wp-block-heading">What should I put on my bathroom counter?</h3>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph">Hand soap, a toothbrush cup and maybe lotion on one small tray, plus one decor piece like a plant, a vase of greenery or a basket of rolled towels. Store everything else.</p>



<h3 class="wp-block-heading">How do I decorate a small bathroom counter?</h3>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph">Keep only soap and a toothbrush cup out, use a narrow shelf above the sink for the toothbrush cup, soap and one small decor piece and move everything else to wall hooks, an over-the-toilet shelf or the cabinet under the sink.</p>



<h3 class="wp-block-heading">How do I make my bathroom counter look expensive?</h3>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph">Use matching glass or ceramic pump bottles, a natural material tray like wood or stone, one fresh or dried green element and plenty of clear space.</p>



<h3 class="wp-block-heading">Should I keep medicines on the bathroom counter?</h3>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph">No. MedlinePlus notes that heat and moisture from the shower, bath and sink may damage medicines, and suggests a cool, dry place such as a dresser drawer or kitchen cabinet, out of reach and out of sight of children, ideally with a child latch or lock.</p>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph">Pretty perfume bottles look lovely on a vanity, but steam and warmth can change the scent over time. Our guide on <a href="https://dailyspacehacks.com/how-to-store-perfume/">how to store perfume</a> explains where to keep the bottles you want to last.</p>



<h2 class="wp-block-heading">Final Thoughts</h2>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph">The best bathroom counter decor is simple: one tray for daily items, one decor piece in a corner, a clear splash zone and safe storage for medicines and hair tools. Start by clearing the counter tonight and putting back only what you use every day.</p>



